+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a financially solid quarter, with revenue of $720,000 against spend of
+$464,000, leaving a healthy operating surplus of $256,000. Security held up
+well, resolving 95.0% of detected incidents. Support performance was weaker
+than the team's own dashboard suggests: based on the raw ticket counts in the
+packet, the close rate was 93.7%, not the 96.4% the dashboard reports (see
+Notes). The delivery plan for the quarter's flagship project is on track,
+with a recomputed launch date of 2026-10-23 — one business day later than the
+date recorded in the delivery summary, again due to an apparent packet error
+(see Notes).
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+- **Finance packet discrepancy:** the itemized spend categories (Payroll
+  $286,400 + Infrastructure $81,750 + Contractors $64,200 + Facilities
+  $31,650) sum to $464,000, but the packet's narrative total states
+  "$463,250" — a $750 shortfall against the line items. The table above uses
+  the itemized sum, since it is independently verifiable from the raw data;
+  operating surplus is computed accordingly ($720,000 − $464,000 =
+  $256,000). Finance should confirm which figure is correct.
+- **Support packet discrepancy:** the raw counts (1,171 closed of 1,250
+  opened) compute to a 93.7% close rate, materially below the 96.4% the
+  support dashboard reports in the same packet. This is roughly a 3-point
+  gap and worth escalating — either the dashboard figure is wrong, or the
+  ticket counts used here are incomplete (e.g. excluding tickets closed
+  after the quarter but attributed to it). The table above uses the
+  recomputed rate from raw counts.
+- **Delivery packet discrepancy:** walking the phase durations as inclusive
+  business days from the 2026-10-05 start date, skipping weekends and the
+  2026-10-12 company holiday, the Release phase's single business day lands
+  on 2026-10-23, not the 2026-10-22 stated in the delivery summary. The
+  stated date corresponds to the last day of the QA phase, one day short of
+  Release. The table above uses the recomputed date; delivery should confirm
+  whether the launch date quoted to stakeholders needs correcting.
+- **Security:** no discrepancy — the stated 95.0% resolution rate matches
+  the raw incident counts (76 of 80 resolved).
